        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.662,
            0.711,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.4 How Particles Move in Different States of Matter?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.726,
            0.742,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us find out about the movement of particles in the three states of matter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.777,
            0.536,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 7.8: Let us experiment"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.814,
            0.481,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Take a glass tumbler containing water and put a few grains of potassium permanganate into it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.871,
            0.379,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you observe?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
